{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"nonlineal-melancholy-grouper","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\n\nParent epic `a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb` (despotic-floriated-leopard). `managed_refs`\n(`src/rebar/reducer/_managed_refs.py`) marks a ref managed the instant it is created LOCALLY and\nis strictly monotonic, so guard G3 in the inbound removal path cannot tell a brand-new\nnever-pushed local link from a peer-deleted one. This story adds the missing evidence store; it\nchanges NO removal behavior (S3 does that).\n\nDirection is fixed by the epic: retain durable association/provenance, never treat an unqualified\nmissing link as deletion evidence. Record shape is a FULL record (vendor link id, direction,\nconfirming pass, confirmed-at), not a boolean — see the epic's \"Chosen direction\" section and the\nepic comment \"Decomposition design calls\" (D1 storage home, D2 key shape, D3 pass_id).\n\n# Scope\n\nNew module `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/peer_confirmations.py`, modelled on the existing\nsidecar `impossible_links.py` (SCHEMA_VERSION constant, `STORE_RELATIVE` path, atomic\nmkstemp + `os.replace` save, tolerant load).\n\n- Store file: `.tickets-tracker/.bridge_state/peer_confirmations.json`.\n- Record key: `(source_local_id, target_local_id, relation)` — relation-scoped, matching\n  `_inbound_unlink_one` (relation-scoped since e39f) and `impossible_links.record_key`.\n- Record fields: `link_id` (vendor link id when the transport supplies one, else null),\n  `direction` (`outbound` when we pushed it | `snapshot` when observed), `confirmed_pass`\n  (pass id), `confirmed_at` (epoch ns), `source` (`push` | `snapshot` | `backfill`).\n- API: `open_store(repo_root)`, `is_confirmed(source, target, relation)`,\n  `record(source, target, relation, *, link_id, direction, pass_id, source_kind)`, `save()`.\n- Write site: `dispatch_one.py::_update_one_dispatch_links`, immediately AFTER the\n  `set_relationship` call succeeds (the engine's sole `set_relationship` call site). The\n  outbound ADD payload already carries `relation`, so no key translation is needed. Recording\n  must not change `_links_computed` / `_links_applied` counters (the silent-no-op canary).\n- Durability: add the new file to the staged `_rel_files` list in\n  `reconcile_helpers.py::_commit_binding_store_snapshot` — omitting it loses the store on every\n  CI checkout (bug b8b1's recorded lesson).\n\nLoading/saving is failure-tolerant (fail-OPEN like `bindings-retired.json`, NOT fail-closed like\n`bindings.json`): a corrupt/absent store must degrade to \"nothing confirmed\" without aborting the\npass. S4 supplies the backfill that makes \"nothing confirmed\" safe.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 `peer_confirmations.py` exists with SCHEMA_VERSION, is <= 400 LOC, and every module it\n      edits stays under the 800-line cap (verify against `git archive HEAD`).\n- [ ] AC2 `record()` then `is_confirmed()` returns True for exactly that\n      `(source, target, relation)` and False for the same pair under a different relation.\n- [ ] AC3 A successful outbound link ADD dispatched through `_update_one_dispatch_links` writes a\n      record with `direction=\"outbound\"`, `source=\"push\"`, the dispatched relation, and the\n      `pass_id`; a FAILED `set_relationship` writes no record.\n- [ ] AC4 Recording leaves `_links_computed` and `_links_applied` byte-identical to pre-change\n      behavior for both the success and the dedup-skip path.\n- [ ] AC5 The store round-trips across a ticket-log SNAPSHOT compaction (behavioral test:\n      confirm, compact the ticket, re-open the store, still confirmed).\n- [ ] AC6 A corrupt or absent `peer_confirmations.json` yields an empty store and does NOT raise.\n- [ ] AC7 `peer_confirmations.json` is in the staged file list of\n      `_commit_binding_store_snapshot`, asserted by test.\n- [ ] AC8 `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; new tests pass.\n\n# Out of scope\n\nSnapshot-sourced confirmation (S2), the removal decline (S3), backfill (S4).","id":"248f-ac00-18db-4259","parent_id":"a4bd-4ca8-c44f-49bb","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Persist a peer-confirmation record per managed link"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786558444278129001,"uuid":"1be1985b-cbae-4ea0-8237-3bca6ab61887"}